# ============================================================================
# Wide table compliance case e03
#
# A test case for core-spec/wide_table_semantics.md, the Wide Table Query
# Interface (Layer 3), as an ost script (apache/ossie#501). The argument to
# executeLower is the query under test, in the JSON binding of Section 3.7.
# executeLower lowers it to a Layer 2 query (Section 5), and the lowering
# raises an error of Section 8. The case requires only the code at the
# start of the error. README.md gives the rules for cases.
#
# Run, from the root of the repository:
#   uv run --project ost ost -d compliance compliance/wide_table/e03_empty_aggregation_query.ost
# ============================================================================

# The "retail" fixture has the tables and values of retail/retail.sql.
connect("retail");
set("doubleDigits", 2);

# The model is retail/retail_model.ossie.yaml.
modelFile("retail_model", "retail/retail_model.ossie.yaml");

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# e03. A query needs a dimension or a metric.
# Question: (A query with only a filter.)
# All parts are optional, but at least one dimension or metric is required.
# Spec: 3.2, 8
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
executeLower("retail_model", {
  "filter": "TRUE"
});
> error: E_EMPTY_AGGREGATION_QUERY: the query has neither dimensions nor metrics

# End e03_empty_aggregation_query.ost
